Note that this program assumes that the user has already set up the necessary AWS credentials and permissions to create the EKS cluster and related resources. The program also uses realistic offline-valid AWS values for attributes such as CIDR blocks, regions/AZ shapes, instance types, DNS-compatible S3 bucket names, Route53 record types, and SSH ingress.

