    ]
  })
}
```
This Terraform configuration creates an MSK cluster with 3 broker nodes, an S3 bucket for storing Kafka data, a Kinesis Firehose delivery stream for streaming data to S3, and a CloudWatch log group for storing Kafka logs. The MSK cluster has encryption at rest and open monitoring enabled. The S3 bucket has versioning enabled and server-side encryption using AES256. The Kinesis Firehose delivery stream has a role that allows it to write to the S3 bucket. The CloudWatch log group has a retention period of 365 days.

