The `aws_eventbridge_event_rule` resource is used to create the event rule, with the `schedule_expression` attribute set to a cron expression that specifies a schedule of every day at 7 UTC.

The `aws_eventbridge_event_target` resource is used to create the event target, with the `rule` attribute set to the name of the event rule, and the `target_id` attribute set to a unique identifier for the event target. The `arn` attribute is set to the ARN of the Lambda function that will be invoked by the event target.

The `aws_lambda_function` resource is used to create the Lambda function, with the `function_name` attribute set to a unique identifier for the Lambda function, and the `role` attribute set to the ARN of the IAM role that will be used to execute the Lambda function. The `filename` attribute is set to the path of the ZIP file containing the Lambda function code, and the `handler` attribute is set to the name of the function handler. The `runtime` attribute is set to the runtime environment for the Lambda function.

The `aws_iam_role` resource is used to create the IAM role that will be used to execute the Lambda function. The `assume_role_policy` attribute is set to a JSON-encoded policy document that allows the Lambda function to assume the role.

The `aws_lambda_permission` resource is used to give the EventBridge event rule permission to invoke the Lambda function. The `action` attribute is set to the action that the event rule will be allowed to perform, and the `function_name` attribute is set to the name of the Lambda function that will be invoked. The `principal` attribute is set to the principal that will be allowed to invoke the Lambda function. The `source_arn` attribute is set to the ARN of the EventBridge event rule that will be allowed to invoke the Lambda function.

