This Terraform program creates the following resources:

* An AWS VPC with the CIDR block 10.0.0.0/16 and DNS hostnames and support enabled.
* An AWS subnet with the CIDR block 10.0.1.0/24 in the us-east-1a availability zone and associated with the VPC.
* An AWS security group with ingress and egress rules allowing traffic on port 3306 from anywhere and all traffic from anywhere, respectively.
* An AWS IAM role with the AssumeRole policy allowing the RDS service to assume the role.
* An AWS Secrets Manager secret with no tags.
* An AWS RDS Aurora MySQL cluster with the engine version 5.7.mysql_aurora.2.10.0, database name "mydb", master username "myuser", and master password "mypassword". The cluster is associated with the VPC, subnet, security group, IAM role, and Secrets Manager secret.
* An AWS RDS Aurora MySQL cluster instance with the instance class "db.r5.large", engine "aurora-mysql", engine version "5.7.mysql_aurora.2.10.0", and associated with the cluster and subnet.
* An AWS RDS proxy with the debug logging disabled, idle client timeout set to 1800 seconds, and associated with the RDS cluster, IAM role, and Secrets Manager secret.

Note that this program does not create any output variables, as the user did not specify any output requirements.

