This Terraform configuration creates a load balancer with a target group for Lambda functions. The load balancer is named "my-load-balancer" and is configured to use the "application" load balancer type. It is associated with two subnets in the "us-east-1" region. The access logs and connection logs are stored in an S3 bucket named "my-load-balancer-logs". The IPAM pool is configured to use the "ipam-pool-12345678" IPAM pool. The minimum load balancer capacity is set to 2. The subnet mapping is configured to use the "subnet-12345678" subnet. The timeouts are set to 10 minutes for create, delete, and update.

The target group is named "my-lambda-target-group" and is configured to use the "HTTP" protocol on port 80. The health check is enabled and checks for a 200 response code on the root path. The stickiness is enabled and uses the "lb_cookie" type with a cookie duration of 86400 seconds and a cookie name of "my-lb-cookie". The target failover is set to terminate the target on deregistration and on unhealthy. The target group health is enabled and the target health state is set to terminate the target on unhealthy connection termination.

The target group attachment is created and associates the "lambda-function-12345678" target with the "my-lambda-target-group" target group on port 80.

