  vpc_id = aws_vpc.vpc.id
  route {
    cidr_block = "0.0.0.0/0"
    gateway_id = aws_internet_gateway.igw.id
  }
  tags = {
    Name = var.name
  }
}

resource "aws_vpc_dhcp_options" "dhcp_options" {
  domain_name = "example.com"
  domain_name_servers = ["AmazonProvidedDNS"]
  netbios_name_servers = ["AmazonProvidedDNS"]
  netbios_node_type = "2"
  ntp_servers = ["169.254.169.123"]
  tags = {
    Name = var.name
  }
}

resource "aws_vpc_dhcp_options_association" "dhcp_options_association" {
  vpc_id = aws_vpc.vpc.id
  dhcp_options_id = aws_vpc_dhcp_options.dhcp_options.id
}
```
This Terraform program defines the following resources:

* `aws_vpc`: A dedicated-tenancy AWS VPC with DNS support and hostnames enabled.
* `aws_internet_gateway`: An internet gateway for the VPC.
* `aws_route_table`: A route table for outbound internet access.
* `aws_route`: A route for outbound internet access.
* `aws_vpc_dhcp_options`: DHCP options for the VPC.
* `aws_vpc_dhcp_options_association`: DHCP options association for the VPC.

The program uses the `aws` provider to configure the AWS region and the `variable` block to define the `name` variable with a default value of `my-vpc`. The `aws_vpc` resource is defined with a CIDR block of `10.0.0.0/16`, DNS support and hostnames enabled, and a tag with the `Name` key set to the value of the `name` variable. The `aws_internet_gateway` resource is defined with a VPC ID set to the ID of the `aws_vpc` resource and a tag with the `Name` key set to the value of the `name` variable. The `aws_route_table` resource is defined with a VPC ID set to the ID of the `aws_vpc` resource and a route with a CIDR block of `0.0.0.0/0` and a gateway ID set to the ID of the `aws_internet_gateway` resource. The `aws_vpc_dhcp_options` resource is defined with domain name `example.com`, domain name servers `AmazonProvidedDNS`, netbios name servers `AmazonProvidedDNS`, netbios node type `2`, and NTP servers `169.254.169.123`. The `aws_vpc_dhcp_options_association` resource is defined with a VPC ID set to the ID of the `aws_vpc` resource and a DHCP options ID set to the ID of the `aws_vpc_dhcp_options` resource.

Note that this Terraform program assumes that the `aws_vpc` resource is already created and that the `aws_internet_gateway` resource is created in the same region as the `aws_vpc` resource. If these resources are not already created, you will need to modify the program accordingly.

